>=20
Tony,

The three configs represent the memory models FLATMEM, DISCONTIGMEM, and=20
SPARSEMEM.  The first two demonstrate what is minimally required in a confi=
g=20
for the memory model of interest.  The SPARSEMEM config is defconfig modifi=
ed=20
for SPARSEMEM memory model and config generated. You can use other permutat=
ions
to generate a MEMORY model but didn't see any point in providing because
the current defconfigs demonstrate this for FLATMEM and DISCONTIGMEM.

I had a problem booting sparsemem_defconfig without modules on my rx2600.
After removing CONFIG_SGI_MBCS it booted fine.

